CORE
main.c
--32 --no-assertions --datarace --unwind 2 --rounds 2 --no-por
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
Thread 1 stores B[0], thread 3 stores B[M]; with M == 0 they race. The store
at the undecided index is a guarded store per element, and the elements it
does not reach were framed back from a stale whole-array version, which hid
the race. Missed (SUCCESSFUL) before the array old-value fix, FAILED after.
See store_at_index_race_safe (M >= 1), which must stay SUCCESSFUL.
